<title>UK: Sears active after agency cross trade.</title>
<headline>Sears active after agency cross trade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in UK retailer Sears Plc were the most actively traded in London on Friday after a large agency cross trade, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said 69.5 million shares were traded at 58p, a fresh low.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe the shares went from one set of hands to another,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>At 1415 GMT, the shares were down 2-1/2p to 59. --London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
